---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy and User Data Protection Statement">

	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<p class="update-date">Last updated: July 26, 2026</p>

	<!-- ==========================================
	🔏 Privacy Policy — The following is a general template. Please modify it to fit your actual product.
	========================================== -->

	<section>
		<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
		<p>
			We ("we", "us", or "the Product") recognize the importance of personal information to you and will take appropriate security measures in accordance with applicable laws and regulations to protect your personal information.
			This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and share your personal information, and how you can manage such information.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
		<p>In the course of using our product, we may collect the following types of information:</p>
		<ul>
			<!-- 👇 Modify the data types collected based on your actual product -->
			<li>
				<strong>Account Information:</strong>
				When you register an account, we may collect your username, email address, and similar information.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Usage Data:</strong>
				We may automatically collect information about how you use the product, including access times, features used, operation logs, etc.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Device Information:</strong>
				We may collect device model, operating system version, unique device identifiers, and similar information.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Content You Provide:</strong>
				When you create, upload, or share content using the product, we may need to collect such content to provide our services.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
		<p>The information we collect will be used for the following purposes:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Providing, maintaining, and improving our product and services.</li>
			<li>Processing your registration, login, and account management.</li>
			<li>Sending you service-related notifications (such as updates, security alerts, etc.).</li>
			<li>Analyzing and researching usage trends to improve user experience.</li>
			<li>Detecting, preventing, and resolving technical issues or abuse.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>
		<p>
			We adopt industry-standard security measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure, use, modification, damage, or loss.
			While we strive to protect your personal information, please note that no security measure is absolutely secure.
		</p>
		<p>
			We retain your personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes described in this policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>5. Information Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
		<p>We do not sell your personal information to third parties. We share your information only in the following circumstances:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>With your explicit consent.</strong></li>
			<li><strong>With our service providers:</strong> To implement specific functionalities (such as cloud storage or data analytics), we may share necessary information with our partners.</li>
			<li><strong>Legal requirements:</strong> Disclosure required by laws, regulations, judicial proceedings, or government requests.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
		<p>
			Under applicable data protection laws, you may have the following rights:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Right of Access:</strong> You may request access to the personal information we hold about you.</li>
			<li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> You may request correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal information.</li>
			<li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> In certain circumstances, you may request deletion of your personal information.</li>
			<li><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> You may withdraw your consent to data processing at any time.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			To exercise these rights, please contact us at <a href="mailto:your@email.com">your@email.com</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>
		<p>
			The product may contain links to third-party websites or services. We assume no responsibility for third-party privacy practices,
			and we recommend that you review the privacy policies of the relevant third parties.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			This product is not intended for children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
			If we become aware that such information has been collected, we will delete it promptly.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>9. Updates to This Policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The updated version will be published on this page,
			and material changes will be communicated to you through appropriate means (such as in-app notifications or email).
			Please check this page periodically for the latest version.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
		<p>
			If you have any questions, comments, or complaints about this Privacy Policy, please contact us through the following channels:
		</p>
		<ul class="contact-info">
			<li>📧 Email: <a href="mailto:your@email.com">your@email.com</a></li>
			<!-- 👇 Add more contact methods -->
		</ul>
	</section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.update-date {
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}
	section {
		margin-bottom: 2.5em;
	}
	section h2 {
		text-align: left;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	section h2::after {
		display: none;
	}
	section p,
	section li {
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		line-height: 1.8;
	}
	section ul {
		padding-left: 1.5em;
	}
	section li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.contact-info {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
	}
</style>
